From: Pyra developer <dev@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] pvrsgx: let the SGX power domain go off at idle

pvr_probe takes a runtime-PM reference and only pvr_remove gives it back,
so the SGX, its ti-sysc module and PD_GPU stay on for as long as the
driver is bound. Active power management is compiled in and balances its
own get/put, but it can only ever bring the count down to 1.

Measured on a Pyra: runtime_usage 1 at desktop idle, runtime_suspended_time
0 after hours, PD_GPU ON-ACTIVE. With the module unloaded PD_GPU reaches
OFF and the battery draw falls by 0.22 W.

Drop the probe reference once the driver is up. SysInitialise has already
taken and released its own, and every later hardware access goes through
EnableSGXClocks, which takes one.

APM releases 2 ms after the SGX goes idle, so use autosuspend (100 ms,
tunable through power/autosuspend_delay_ms) so that the domain is not
power-cycled between frames.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.14.3699939/eurasia_km/services4/system/omap/sysutils_linux.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.14.3699939/eurasia_km/services4/system/omap/sysutils_linux.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.14.3699939/eurasia_km/services4/system/omap/sysutils_linux.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.14.3699939/eurasia_km/services4/system/omap/sysutils_linux.c
@@ -261,10 +261,17 @@
 
 #if defined(LDM_PLATFORM) && !defined(PVR_DRI_DRM_NOT_PCI)
 	{
-		int res = pm_runtime_put_sync(&gpsPVRLDMDev->dev);
+		/*
+		 * Autosuspend, not put_sync: the domain goes off only once the
+		 * SGX has stayed idle for the delay set in pvr-drv.c.
+		 */
+		int res;
+
+		pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(&gpsPVRLDMDev->dev);
+		res = pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(&gpsPVRLDMDev->dev);
 		if (res < 0)
 		{
-			PVR_DPF((PVR_DBG_ERROR, "DisableSGXClocks: pm_runtime_put_sync failed (%d)", -res));
+			PVR_DPF((PVR_DBG_ERROR, "DisableSGXClocks: pm_runtime_put_autosuspend failed (%d)", -res));
 		}
 	}
 #if defined(SYS_OMAP_HAS_DVFS_FRAMEWORK)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/pvr-drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/pvr-drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/pvr-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/pvr-drv.c
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 
+/* How long the SGX must stay idle before its power domain is allowed to go off. */
+#define PVR_AUTOSUSPEND_MS	100
+
 #include <drm/drm.h>
 #include <drm/drm_device.h>
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
@@ -292,6 +295,23 @@
 
 	gpsPVRLDMDev = pdev;
 
+	/*
+	 * Drop the reference taken above. SysInitialise has taken and released
+	 * its own by now ("SGX defaults to D3"), and every later hardware access
+	 * goes through EnableSGXClocks, which takes one. Holding this one kept the
+	 * SGX, its ti-sysc module and PD_GPU powered for as long as the driver was
+	 * bound, so active power management could never power anything down.
+	 *
+	 * APM releases its reference 2 ms after the SGX goes idle, which would
+	 * power-cycle the domain between frames. With autosuspend the domain only
+	 * goes off after PVR_AUTOSUSPEND_MS of quiet; power/autosuspend_delay_ms
+	 * tunes it at run time.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(ddata->dev, PVR_AUTOSUSPEND_MS);
+	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(ddata->dev);
+	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(ddata->dev);
+	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(ddata->dev);
+
 	return 0;
 
 out_err_unload:
@@ -313,7 +333,8 @@
 	pvr_drm_unload(gpsPVRDRMDev);
 	gpsPVRDRMDev = NULL;
 
-	pm_runtime_put_sync(&pdev->dev);
+	/* The probe reference was dropped at the end of probe. */
+	pm_runtime_dont_use_autosuspend(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
 
 	return 0;
